  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Hei Lou Lan says the heavenly road feels like something depicted in The Legends of Ren Zu, and Lu Tong Lan names it Upslope Road and Downslope Road. Lu Tong Lan agrees, and says whether the Gu she has in mind exist here depends on fortune, and that if they do they will be near the end of the heavenly road. Immortal Zombie Giant Sun’s guidance is to avoid the Downslope Road and walk the Upslope Road. She and Lu Tong Lan try that as much as they can. Most of what they find at first is mortal Gu and materials. When they find the first rank six Immortal Gu, the first Predicament also appears.",
        "chapters": [
          2115
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_hei_lou_lan",
          "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
          "char_lu_tong_lan",
          "loc_upslope_road",
          "loc_downslope_road",
          "char_immortal_zombie_giant_sun",
          "sys_mortal_gu",
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After fortitude Gu, another rank eight Immortal Gu appears on the Upslope Road. Hei Lou Lan names it as another famous Immortal Gu from The Legends of Ren Zu. The rank seven Gu Immortal who already holds fortitude Gu says this one is even better.",
        "chapters": [
          2116
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "heavenly-road-sighting",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_fortitude_gu",
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After Hei Lou Lan, Yellow Bell Tribe Leader, and that rank seven Gu Immortal kill the Predicament, Yellow Bell Tribe Leader claims it as his by sequence. The rank seven Gu Immortal moves first, snatches it from the ground, and places it into his immortal aperture. Hei Lou Lan wants it too, but she is the furthest from it after leaving the Predicament’s body.",
        "chapters": [
          2117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "heavenly-road-snatch",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_yellow_bell_tribe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In The Legends of Ren Zu, because Great Strength True Martial walked the Upslope Road, this Gu suddenly appears within him. He tells Ren Zu it is the result of effort Gu awakening his potential. It speaks, helps defeat Predicaments, and is tossed into tribulation, growing larger and stronger through hurdles. Several days after the ceremony Fang Yuan holds it with fortitude Gu as a pair of rank eight Immortal Gu retrieved by Zhan Bu Du.",
        "chapters": [
          2117
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "heavenly-road-snatch",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_great_strength_true_martial",
          "char_ren_zu",
          "gu_effort_gu",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_zhan_bu_du"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When Ren Zu’s group needs to help him recognize self Gu again, Great Strength True Martial’s ability Gu says that undergoing situations can make it stronger. As he and practice Gu keep undergoing situations, ability Gu grows stronger and the floating ice ball carrying the group grows larger with it, through stages of light, water, and stone membranes, until they reach self Gu at the ice ball’s largest, crystal stage.",
        "chapters": [
          2294
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "undergoing-situations-to-find-self-gu",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_self_gu",
          "gu_practice_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
